course: dictionary
lesson: 15448
title: Families and the word stepfather
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Families can be made in different ways, and the word stepfather helps us talk about one of them. A stepfather is a man who is married to your mother, but he is not your birth father. «My stepfather taught me to ride my bike last summer.» The sentence tells you he is someone in the family who helps you.
explain: Use the clues in the word and the sentence. The word step shows that the family link comes through marriage, not through birth. «Sam's stepdad and his mum got married in May.» Stepdad is a shorter, friendly word for stepfather, and it means the same thing. To check, put stepfather into the sentence in place of stepdad and see if it still makes sense.
explain: A stepfather can be kind and loving, just like any parent. Some fairy tales show cruel stepparents, but that is a story pattern, not what real families are like. To understand a word about families, read the sentences around it and notice what the people in them do and feel.
fact: A stepfather is a man who is married to your mother but is not your birth father.
fact: «Stepdad» is an informal, friendly word for stepfather.
fact: Families come in many shapes, with stepfathers, stepmothers, stepbrothers and stepsisters.
fact: A stepfather can be a loving parent in real life.
fact: Cruel stepparents often appear in fairy tales, but that is a story trope, not the truth about real families.
exercise: «My stepfather taught me to ride my bike.» What is a stepfather? | A teacher at your school | *A man married to your mother who is not your birth father | Your birth father, who lives far away | Your mum's best friend
exercise: Sam says, «My stepdad is kind.» What does stepdad mean? | A man who fixes cars | *A stepfather, a man married to your mum | A brother of your dad | A grandfather
exercise: Maya's stepfather makes pancakes every Sunday. What is the family link between Maya and him? | *He is married to Maya's mum but is not her birth father | Her cousin | Her teacher | Her birth father
test: Lily says, «My stepfather and my mum got married on a beach.» Who is Lily's stepfather? | A man who is Lily's birth father | Lily's uncle | *A man married to Lily's mum who is not her birth father | A boy in Lily's class
test: Ben says, «My stepdad and I play football in the park.» Which sentence best explains stepdad? | Stepdad is Ben's birth father | *Stepdad is an informal word for stepfather, a man married to Ben's mum | Stepdad means a teacher who runs a football club | Stepdad means a park keeper
exam: «Priya's stepfather is a loving parent who reads her a story each night.» What is a stepfather? | Priya's older brother | *A man married to Priya's mum who is not her birth father | A stranger who lives on Priya's street | A man who is not married to anyone
